# US-4127 — Update order status from the order detail page

## User story

As a customer support agent, I want to set an order's status to "Shipped" from the order detail page, so that I stop emailing the logistics team for every update.

## Business context

Support handles roughly 400 status updates per week over email. Each hand-off takes 20–40 minutes and sometimes gets lost between inboxes. Letting agents update the status directly should remove most of that manual work and cut the delay between dispatch and the customer seeing "Shipped" from hours to minutes.

## Acceptance criteria

- An agent with the Support role can change an order's status to Shipped from the order detail page.
- The change records the timestamp of the status update.
- The endpoint rejects requests from users without the Support role.

Code diff the description refers to:

diff --git a/src/Api/Controllers/OrdersController.cs b/src/Api/Controllers/OrdersController.cs
index 4a1c9f2..b7e3d10 100644
--- a/src/Api/Controllers/OrdersController.cs
+++ b/src/Api/Controllers/OrdersController.cs
@@ -28,6 +28,17 @@ public sealed class OrdersController : ControllerBase
         return Ok(order);
     }

+    [HttpPatch("{id:int}/status")]
+    [Authorize(Roles = "Support")]
+    public async Task<IActionResult> UpdateStatus(int id, [FromBody] UpdateOrderStatusRequest request)
+    {
+        var updated = await _orderService.UpdateStatusAsync(id, request.Status, HttpContext.RequestAborted);
+        return updated ? NoContent() : NotFound();
+    }
+
     [HttpDelete("{id:int}")]
     [Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]
     public async Task<IActionResult> Delete(int id)
diff --git a/src/Api/Dtos/UpdateOrderStatusRequest.cs b/src/Api/Dtos/UpdateOrderStatusRequest.cs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e69de29
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/Api/Dtos/UpdateOrderStatusRequest.cs
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;
+
+namespace Shop.Api.Dtos;
+
+public sealed record UpdateOrderStatusRequest(
+    [Required, RegularExpression("^(Pending|Shipped|Delivered|Cancelled)$")]
+    string Status);
diff --git a/src/Application/Orders/OrderService.cs b/src/Application/Orders/OrderService.cs
index 91b2aa4..c4d5e77 100644
--- a/src/Application/Orders/OrderService.cs
+++ b/src/Application/Orders/OrderService.cs
@@ -64,6 +64,19 @@ public sealed class OrderService : IOrderService
         return order;
     }

+    public async Task<bool> UpdateStatusAsync(int orderId, string status, CancellationToken ct)
+    {
+        var order = await _repository.FindByIdAsync(orderId, ct);
+        if (order is null)
+        {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        order.Status = status;
+        order.StatusUpdatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow;
+        await _repository.SaveChangesAsync(ct);
+        return true;
+    }
+
     public async Task DeleteAsync(int orderId, CancellationToken ct)
diff --git a/src/Infrastructure/Migrations/Scripts/20261101_add_status_updated_at.sql b/src/Infrastructure/Migrations/Scripts/20261101_add_status_updated_at.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f7c2d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/Infrastructure/Migrations/Scripts/20261101_add_status_updated_at.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+-- src/Infrastructure/Migrations/Scripts/20261101_add_status_updated_at.sql
+ALTER TABLE Orders ADD StatusUpdatedAt datetime2 NULL;
+GO
diff --git a/tests/Orders/OrdersControllerTests.cs b/tests/Orders/OrdersControllerTests.cs
index 77c1e2b..2f9a8d4 100644
--- a/tests/Orders/OrdersControllerTests.cs
+++ b/tests/Orders/OrdersControllerTests.cs
@@ -41,4 +41,18 @@ public sealed class OrdersControllerTests
         Assert.IsType<OkObjectResult>(result);
     }
+
+    [Fact]
+    public async Task UpdateStatus_ReturnsNoContent_WhenOrderExists()
+    {
+        var service = new Mock<IOrderService>();
+        service.Setup(s => s.UpdateStatusAsync(7, "Shipped", It.IsAny<CancellationToken>()))
+               .ReturnsAsync(true);
+        var controller = new OrdersController(service.Object);
+
+        var result = await controller.UpdateStatus(7, new UpdateOrderStatusRequest("Shipped"));
+
+        Assert.IsType<NoContentResult>(result);
+        service.Verify(s => s.UpdateStatusAsync(7, "Shipped", It.IsAny<CancellationToken>()), Times.Once);
+    }
 }

PR description to grade:

### What is this change?

Adds a Support-role-authorized PATCH endpoint that lets agents update an order's status (e.g., to "Shipped") and records the update timestamp.

### Type of change?

- New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)

### Why?

Support currently handles around 400 order status updates per week by email, with each hand-off taking 20–40 minutes and sometimes getting lost. Letting Support agents update the status directly removes most of that manual work and reduces the delay between dispatch and the customer seeing "Shipped".

### How?

- Adds a nullable `StatusUpdatedAt` column to the `Orders` table via a migration script.
- Adds the `UpdateOrderStatusRequest` DTO with a required `Status` field validated against `Pending`, `Shipped`, `Delivered`, or `Cancelled`.
- Adds `OrderService.UpdateStatusAsync`, which loads the order, sets the new status, assigns `StatusUpdatedAt` to `DateTime.UtcNow`, and saves the changes.
- Adds `PATCH /api/orders/{id}/status` in `OrdersController`, authorized to the `Support` role, returning `204 NoContent` on success or `404 Not Found` when the order does not exist.
- Adds a controller unit test verifying that `UpdateStatus` returns `NoContent` when the order exists.

### Requires Manual Database Migration?

Yes

```sql
ALTER TABLE Orders ADD StatusUpdatedAt datetime2 NULL;
GO
```

### Anything Else?

The `StatusUpdatedAt` column is nullable, so existing orders remain valid without a value. The new endpoint is restricted to the `Support` role and returns `404 Not Found` if the order ID does not exist.

Rubric criterion:

The "Why?" field explains the business reason stated in the User Story (support handling ~400 manual status updates per week, 20-40 minute hand-offs, hours-to-minutes delay), not a restatement of the code change.


